// Handling failures in application code: the till decides what each of
// `price_basket`'s failures means for a sale.

/// What the till charges for `basket`. An old or mistyped code shouldn't
/// stop a sale, so the till charges full price instead, and the customer
/// can ask about the code afterwards. An empty basket, or a code worth
/// more than the basket, still stops it.
action till_total(basket: Basket) fails BasketEmpty, DiscountTooLarge -> Pence {
    return match price_basket(basket) {
        success(receipt) -> receipt.total
        // Recovering: the same lines at full price. A handled failure
        // leaves the `fails` list, so `CodeUnknown` isn't in this one.
        CodeUnknown -> price_lines(basket)
        // `propagate` passes these on unchanged, for the caller to handle.
        BasketEmpty -> propagate
        DiscountTooLarge -> propagate
    }
}
